cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use evo-skillopt in a published work, please cite it as follows."
title: "evo-skillopt: text-space skill optimization for production LLM agents"
abstract: >
  A self-hostable HTTP service that evolves a bot's Markdown skill file
  against a held-out eval set using the SkillOpt algorithm. Trains
  natural-language skill contracts like neural-network weights — epochs,
  batches, validation gates — without touching model weights, and
  records every evolution as a git-tracked audit trail.
type: software
authors:
  - name: "evo-skillopt contributors"
    website: "https://github.com/dnzengou/evo-skillopt"
repository-code: "https://github.com/dnzengou/evo-skillopt"
url: "https://dnzengou.github.io/evo-skillopt"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - agent
  - large-language-models
  - prompt-optimization
  - skill-learning
  - evaluation
  - agentic
references:
  - type: article
    title: "SkillOpt: optimizing text-space skill contracts for LLM agents"
    authors:
      - name: "SkillOpt authors"
    url: "https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.23904"
    notes: "The upstream algorithm this project productizes (MIT-licensed)."
